{%- comment -%}
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  pf-contact-form  —  the "Everything else" enquiry form
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Drop-in replacement for the <section id="c-enquiry"> block on the
  contact page. Paste the whole file into that Custom Liquid block, or
  save it as snippets/pf-contact-form.liquid and render it there.

  Plain <style> and <script> rather than {% stylesheet %} / {% javascript %}
  so it works inside a Custom Liquid block, which does not accept those.

  WHAT WAS WRONG WITH THE OLD MARKUP
    1. <form> had no action and no method. It posted to the current URL
       as a GET, put every answer in the address bar and reloaded the
       page. Nothing was ever sent to anyone. This is now a real
       {% form 'contact' %}, so submissions land in the store's inbox.
    2. "Your name" had no name attribute, so even a working form could
       not have submitted it.
    3. Every label both wrapped its input AND carried for="…" — the
       double association that puts the * on its own line as soon as the
       page CSS makes a label a flex column. Labels and inputs are now
       siblings, with one for="…" each.
    4. form_started_at, the honeypot and the success panel existed but
       nothing read or wrote them. All three are live now.
    5. enq-intro-help / enq-email-help / enq-link-help had ids but no
       field pointed at them, so screen readers never announced them.
       Wired up with aria-describedby.
    6. The fabric select held one option, "Not sure yet".

  VALIDATION
    pf-forms.js — data-pf-email gets format, typo-suggestion, disposable
    blocklist and a live MX lookup on the domain; data-pf-phone gets the
    country picker and that country's mobile-length rules. Fetched on the
    first focus in the form, not on page load, so a visitor who scrolls
    past pays nothing. Native validation is the fallback if it never
    arrives, so `required` always bites.

  THE CHECKSUM — read this before relying on it
    Three gates run before submit: the honeypot must be empty, at least
    3s must have passed since the form was first touched, and a token
    derived from that timestamp must match. Passing writes
    contact[Verification] into the submission.

    What this genuinely gives you: every real submission arrives with a
    Verification line, so anything in your inbox WITHOUT one was posted
    straight at Shopify's endpoint by a bot that never ran this page's
    JavaScript. That makes spam filterable at a glance.

    What it cannot do: stop that direct POST. No client-side check can —
    the verifying code would have to run on a server we do not control
    here. For that, switch on Shopify's own captcha in
    Settings → Customer privacy. This layer stops form-filler bots and
    labels the rest.
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # The page already links to /collections/all-fabrics, so prefer it and
  # fall back to every product rather than shipping an empty select.
  assign pfc_fabrics = collections['all-fabrics'].products
  if pfc_fabrics.size == 0
    assign pfc_fabrics = collections.all.products
  endif
  assign pfc_today = 'now' | date: '%Y-%m-%d'
-%}

<section class="pfc-band pfc-band--cream" id="c-enquiry">
  <div class="pfc-section">
    <div class="pfc-section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="pfc-eyebrow">
          <span class="pfc-cmyk"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span> General enquiries
        </p>
        <h2 class="pfc-title" id="c-enquiry-h">Everything else</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pfc-prose">
      <p>
        Use the form for anything the five routes above don't cover. The more of it you fill in, the more
        useful the first reply.
      </p>
    </div>

    {% form 'contact', id: 'enquiry-form', class: 'pfc-form', novalidate: 'novalidate' %}
      {%- comment -%}
        The success panel has to live INSIDE this block. The `form` object only
        exists between form/endform — outside it `form.posted_successfully?` is
        nil, so a panel placed above would never once have appeared.

        Rendered server-side from the redirect, so it is right before any
        JavaScript runs. The fields stay below it, ready for a second enquiry.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
        <p class="pfc-form__success" id="enq-success" role="status" tabindex="-1">
          <strong>Sent.</strong> Quotes are answered the same working day, Monday to Friday.
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if form.errors -%}
        <p class="pfc-form__error" role="alert">
          {{ form.errors | default_errors }}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <p class="pfc-form__help" id="enq-intro-help">
        Fields marked <span class="pfc-req" aria-hidden="true">*</span> are required.
      </p>

      {%- comment -%}
        Anti-bot. The honeypot is off-screen, out of the tab order and
        hidden from assistive tech, so only a script fills it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="pfc-hp" aria-hidden="true">
        <label for="enq-website">Website</label>
        <input id="enq-website" name="website" type="text" autocomplete="off" tabindex="-1">
      </div>
      <input type="hidden" name="form_started_at" value="" data-pfc-started>
      <input type="hidden" name="contact[Verification]" value="" data-pfc-check>

      <div class="pfc-form__row">
        <div class="pfc-field">
          <label class="pfc-field__label" for="enq-name">
            Your name <span class="pfc-req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
          </label>
          <input
            class="pfc-field__input"
            id="enq-name"
            name="contact[name]"
            type="text"
            required
            autocomplete="name"
          >
        </div>

        <div class="pfc-field">
          <label class="pfc-field__label" for="enq-email">
            Email <span class="pfc-req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
          </label>
          <input
            class="pfc-field__input"
            id="enq-email"
            name="contact[email]"
            type="email"
            required
            autocomplete="email"
            inputmode="email"
            aria-describedby="enq-email-help"
            data-pf-email
            data-pf-required
          >
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="pfc-form__help" id="enq-email-help">
        Quotes are answered the same working day, Monday to Friday.
      </p>

      <div class="pfc-form__row">
        <div class="pfc-field">
          <label class="pfc-field__label" for="enq-phone">Phone</label>
          <input
            class="pfc-field__input"
            id="enq-phone"
            name="contact[phone]"
            type="tel"
            autocomplete="tel"
            data-pf-phone
          >
        </div>

        <div class="pfc-field">
          <label class="pfc-field__label" for="enq-country">
            Delivery country <span class="pfc-req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
          </label>
          <select
            class="pfc-field__input"
            id="enq-country"
            name="contact[Delivery country]"
            required
            autocomplete="country-name"
          >
            <option value="">Select…</option>
            <option>USA</option>
            <option>UK</option>
            <option>EU</option>
            <option>Australia</option>
            <option>New Zealand</option>
            <option>Canada</option>
            <option>Other</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pfc-field">
        <label class="pfc-field__label" for="enq-project">
          What are you making <span class="pfc-req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
        </label>
        <input
          class="pfc-field__input"
          id="enq-project"
          name="contact[Project]"
          type="text"
          required
          autocomplete="off"
          placeholder="Trade show backdrop, café window, exhibition wall…"
        >
      </div>

      <div class="pfc-field">
        <label class="pfc-field__label" for="enq-fabric">Fabric, if you've chosen one</label>
        <select class="pfc-field__input" id="enq-fabric" name="contact[Fabric]" autocomplete="off">
          <option value="">Not sure yet</option>
          {%- for pfc_product in pfc_fabrics limit: 40 -%}
            <option value="{{ pfc_product.title | escape }}">{{ pfc_product.title }}</option>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </select>
      </div>

      <div class="pfc-form__row">
        <div class="pfc-field">
          <label class="pfc-field__label" for="enq-size">Finished size, in ft, in or cm</label>
          <input
            class="pfc-field__input"
            id="enq-size"
            name="contact[Finished size]"
            type="text"
            autocomplete="off"
            placeholder="10 ft × 12 ft, or 300 × 200 cm"
          >
        </div>

        <div class="pfc-field">
          <label class="pfc-field__label" for="enq-date">Date you need it</label>
          <input
            class="pfc-field__input"
            id="enq-date"
            name="contact[Date needed]"
            type="date"
            autocomplete="off"
            min="{{ pfc_today }}"
          >
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pfc-field">
        <label class="pfc-field__label" for="enq-message">
          Your question <span class="pfc-req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
        </label>
        <textarea
          class="pfc-field__input pfc-field__input--area"
          id="enq-message"
          name="contact[body]"
          rows="5"
          required
          minlength="10"
        ></textarea>
      </div>

      <div class="pfc-field">
        <label class="pfc-field__label" for="enq-link">Link to your artwork, if you have one</label>
        <input
          class="pfc-field__input"
          id="enq-link"
          name="contact[Artwork link]"
          type="url"
          autocomplete="url"
          inputmode="url"
          aria-describedby="enq-link-help"
          placeholder="https://…"
        >
      </div>

      <p class="pfc-form__help" id="enq-link-help">
        Don't attach files here. Paste a Dropbox, Drive or WeTransfer link instead, or upload directly on
        the fabric page you're ordering.
      </p>

      <div class="pfc-btnrow">
        <button class="btn btn-primary pfc-form__submit" type="submit">Submit enquiry</button>
      </div>

      <p class="pfc-form__error" data-pfc-formerror role="alert" hidden></p>
    {% endform %}
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Everything is scoped under #enquiry-form and wins on specificity, not on
     source order — the page's own `.pfc-form label { flex-direction: column }`
     is what was dropping the asterisk onto its own line, and a rule that only
     won by coming later would break again the next time the CSS is rebuilt. */
  #enquiry-form {
    --pfc-magenta: #e20a6e;
    --pfc-ink: #141c33;
    --pfc-line: #d7dbe6;
    --pfc-muted: #6b7488;
    --pfc-gap: 18px;

    display: block;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  /* Fields are label + control siblings, so the label stays one line and the
     asterisk stays inline with the words. */
  #enquiry-form .pfc-field {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 7px;
    min-width: 0;
    margin-bottom: var(--pfc-gap);
  }

  #enquiry-form .pfc-field__label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--pfc-ink);
  }

  #enquiry-form .pfc-req {
    display: inline;
    color: var(--pfc-magenta);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* Two across on desktop, stacked once there is no room for two. */
  #enquiry-form .pfc-form__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0 var(--pfc-gap);
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 640px) {
    #enquiry-form .pfc-form__row {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }

  #enquiry-form .pfc-field__input {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 46px;
    padding: 11px 13px;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--pfc-line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--pfc-ink);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 1rem; /* never below 16px — iOS zooms the page on focus */
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  #enquiry-form select.pfc-field__input {
    /* Room for the native arrow, and no text sitting under it. */
    padding-inline-end: 34px;
    appearance: none;
    background-image: linear-gradient(45deg, transparent 50%, var(--pfc-muted) 50%),
      linear-gradient(135deg, var(--pfc-muted) 50%, transparent 50%);
    background-position: calc(100% - 19px) center, calc(100% - 13px) center;
    background-size: 6px 6px, 6px 6px;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
  }

  #enquiry-form .pfc-field__input--area {
    min-height: 128px;
    resize: vertical;
  }

  #enquiry-form .pfc-field__input:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--pfc-magenta);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgb(226 10 110 / 14%);
  }

  /* The theme nulls outline globally; keyboard users still need a ring. */
  #enquiry-form :is(input, select, textarea, button):focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--pfc-magenta) !important;
    outline-offset: 2px !important;
  }

  #enquiry-form .pfc-form__help {
    margin: -6px 0 var(--pfc-gap);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--pfc-muted);
  }

  #enquiry-form .pfc-form__submit {
    min-height: 48px;
  }

  #enquiry-form .pfc-form__error {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #c1085d;
  }

  #enquiry-form .pfc-form__error[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Honeypot. Off-screen rather than display:none — a bot that skips hidden
     inputs will still fill this one. */
  #enquiry-form .pfc-hp {
    position: absolute;
    left: -9999px;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .pfc-form__success {
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-inline-start: 3px solid #0899b4;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: #f0f7f9;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #141c33;
  }

  /* Field flagged by pf-forms.js */
  #enquiry-form [data-pf-state='bad'] .pfc-field__input {
    border-color: #c1085d;
  }
</style>

<script>
  (function () {
    'use strict';

    var form = document.getElementById('enquiry-form');
    if (!form) return;

    var MIN_SECONDS = 3;
    var started = form.querySelector('[data-pfc-started]');
    var check = form.querySelector('[data-pfc-check]');
    var honeypot = form.querySelector('#enq-website');
    var errorLine = form.querySelector('[data-pfc-formerror]');

    /* Stamped from the client, not from Liquid: a cached page would hand every
       visitor the same server-side timestamp. */
    var openedAt = Date.now();
    if (started) started.value = String(openedAt);

    /* Move focus to the confirmation after the redirect, otherwise a keyboard
       or screen-reader user lands back at the top of a long page with no idea
       the send worked. */
    var sent = document.getElementById('enq-success');
    if (sent) sent.focus({ preventScroll: true });

    /* Cheap deterministic token over the timestamp. Its job is not secrecy —
       it is a marker proving this page's script ran. See the file header. */
    function token(value) {
      var h = 2166136261;
      var s = String(value);
      for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {
        h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);
        h = (h * 16777619) >>> 0;
      }
      return h.toString(36);
    }

    /* pf-forms.js is ~40 KB. Fetch it the first time someone actually starts
       filling the form in, so a visitor who only reads the page pays nothing. */
    var requested = false;
    function loadValidation() {
      if (requested || window.PFForms) return;
      requested = true;
      var script = document.createElement('script');
      script.src = {{ 'pf-forms.js' | asset_url | json }};
      script.onload = function () {
        if (window.PFForms && window.PFForms.init) window.PFForms.init(form);
      };
      document.head.appendChild(script);
    }

    form.addEventListener('focusin', loadValidation, { once: true });
    form.addEventListener('pointerdown', loadValidation, { once: true });

    function fail(message) {
      if (!errorLine) return;
      errorLine.textContent = message;
      errorLine.hidden = false;
    }

    form.addEventListener('submit', function (event) {
      if (errorLine) errorLine.hidden = true;

      /* 1. Honeypot. Nothing a person can see, so a value means a script. */
      if (honeypot && honeypot.value.trim() !== '') {
        event.preventDefault();
        return;
      }

      /* 2. Nobody reads this page and fills seven fields in three seconds. */
      var elapsed = (Date.now() - openedAt) / 1000;
      if (elapsed < MIN_SECONDS) {
        event.preventDefault();
        fail('That was quicker than a person can type — give it a moment and press Submit again.');
        return;
      }

      /* 3. Native rules first: required, type=email, minlength, type=url. */
      var valid = form.checkValidity();
      if (!valid) form.reportValidity();

      /* 4. Then pf-forms on the email and phone, when it is loaded. */
      if (window.PFForms && window.PFForms.check) {
        Array.prototype.forEach.call(form.querySelectorAll('[data-pf-email],[data-pf-phone]'), function (field) {
          if (!window.PFForms.check(field)) valid = false;
        });
      }

      /* 5. A warning on screen must always beat a passing check. pf-forms'
            email domain lookup is async: it returns true for a well-formed
            address, then paints the failure a moment later without touching
            the input's class. Its message node carries both verdicts, so this
            is what makes "warned but submitted anyway" impossible. */
      if (form.querySelector('.pff-msg.pff-t-bad, .pff-bad')) valid = false;

      if (!valid) {
        event.preventDefault();
        fail('Please check the highlighted fields and try again.');
        return;
      }

      /* 6. Passed everything — stamp the submission so a real one is
            distinguishable from a direct POST that skipped this script. */
      if (check) {
        check.value = 'ok · ' + elapsed.toFixed(1) + 's · ' + token(openedAt);
      }
    });
  })();
</script>
